# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  THIS IS A DELIBERATELY DEFECTIVE FIXTURE. NOT THE REPOSITORY'S GITIGNORE ║
# ║  Do not copy it to /.gitignore. Do not "fix" it — its defect is the point.║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# It is the known-bad input for scripts/check-gitignore-proof.sh, which proves
# that scripts/check-gitignore.sh can actually FAIL. A check that has only ever
# returned PASS is indistinguishable from one that cannot fail, so the sweep is
# worth nothing without a known-bad case to run it against.
#
# The defect, preserved on purpose: the node key-material patterns are
# root-anchored (/keystore/, /wallet.json, /mnemonic.txt) and there is no
# UTC--* pattern. A node run with any datadir other than the repository root --
# `--datadir ./data` -- therefore leaves an encrypted keystore and a plaintext
# BIP-39 mnemonic committable. That was the live state of /.gitignore until
# 2026-08-02, when an adversarial review reproduced it end to end.
#
# If a future change to /.gitignore stops this fixture failing the sweep, the
# sweep has lost the ability to detect that class and the fixture needs
# updating -- not the other way round.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (original header of the defective file follows)
#
# fukuii-cli — .gitignore
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. This file is the gate between what stays local and
# what the world sees. Never weaken a SECURITY block below; add repo-specific
# ignores under the marked section at the bottom.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# == SECURITY: secrets & credentials ==
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
service-account.json
*.credentials
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret

# == SECURITY: package-registry auth ==
# These carry registry auth tokens (`_authToken`, `npmAuthIdent`). A committed
# .npmrc can also silently weaken install-time supply-chain settings.
.npmrc
.yarnrc
.yarnrc.yml

# == SECURITY: node / chain key material ==
# Root-anchored deliberately. These are node-DATADIR artifacts: a node run in the
# repo root writes them at root level, so anchoring covers the whole threat while
# leaving nested paths visible.
#
# Unanchored, `keystore/` swallows the `org.fukuii.…keystore` SOURCE PACKAGE — six
# such files were tracked source in the pre-rebuild tree (KeyStore, Wallet,
# EncryptedKey, EncryptedKeyJsonCodec + two specs). Verified by effect, both
# directions, before this was changed. Do not un-anchor without re-checking.
#
# `*.nodekey` stays global: it is an extension glob, not a datadir path, and no
# source file legitimately carries it.
/keystore/
/wallet.json
/mnemonic.txt
*.nodekey
/node.key
/jwt.hex
/jwtsecret

# == SECURITY: infra / cloud ==
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
*.kubeconfig
kubeconfig
.pgpass
docker-compose.override.yml

# == Local working files — never travel ==
.local/
SESSION_NOTES.md
PLANNING.md
SCRATCH.md
*.scratch.*
*.draft.*

# == Claude Code ==
# This directory is TRACKED so repo-local agents, skills and rules travel with the
# repo. Only machine-local and agent-written state is held back. Do not invert this
# into a blanket ignore: an agent inside an ignored directory never reaches a clone.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/launch.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/**/*.local.*
.claude/**/*-local/

